### Practical 7: Authentication & Middleware Pipeline REST Client Tests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Server Health Check (Returns 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Register New User (Returns 201 Created)
# Tip: If this returns 400 "already exists", either change the email below (e.g. manan1@charusat.edu.in) 
# or jump directly to Request #4 (Login) which returns 200 OK!
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Manan Vasani",
  "email": "manan1@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Register Validation Failure (Testing 400 Bad Request - Password < 6 chars)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "invalid@test.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4. Login User (Returns 200 OK & JWT Token)
# CLICK SEND REQUEST HERE TO GET YOUR 200 OK SCREENSHOT!
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manan@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Attempt Protected Route WITHOUT Token (Testing 401 Unauthorized)
# CLICK SEND REQUEST HERE TO GET YOUR 401 UNAUTHORIZED SCREENSHOT!
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 6. Get Current User Profile (Returns 200 OK with Bearer Token)
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 7. Get Tasks (Returns 200 OK with Bearer Token)
# CLICK SEND REQUEST HERE TO GET YOUR PROTECTED 200 OK SCREENSHOT!
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Create Task (Returns 201 Created with Bearer Token)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Implement JWT Middleware",
  "description": "Practical 7 Authentication & Authorization",
  "priority": "high",
  "completed": false
}

### 9. Task Validation Failure (Testing 400 Bad Request - Missing Title)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "This should fail because title is required"
}

### 10. Update Task by ID (Returns 200 OK)
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body._id}}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true,
  "priority": "medium"
}

### 11. Delete Task by ID (Returns 200 OK)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json
